    Scenario 03 reproduces only the sectors needed through Phase 6:
      Wretched Skies V Family Phi (vanilla Cluster 403)
      Wretched Skies IV Family Valka (vanilla Cluster 400)
      Family Zhin (vanilla Cluster 401)
      Family Nhuut (vanilla Cluster 418 Sector 001)
      Zyarth's Dominion I (vanilla Cluster 404 Sector 001)

    Family Phi landmark mapping used by the screenplay:
      A = Zone003, connection_ClusterGate403To400 (Family Valka)
      B = Zone002, connection_ClusterGate403To422 (Wretched Skies X)
      C = Zone005, connection_ClusterGate403To031 (Heretic's End)

    Family Valka:
      A = Zone001, connection_ClusterGate400To403 (Family Phi)
      B = Zone004, connection_ClusterGate400To401 (Family Zhin)

    Family Zhin:
      A = Zone001, connection_ClusterGate401To400 (Family Valka)
      B = Zone005, connection_ClusterGate401To032 (Tharka's Cascade)
      C = Zone003, connection_ClusterGate401To418 (Family Nhuut)
      D = Zone002, connection_ClusterGate401To402 (Family Kritt)

    Family Nhuut:
      A = Zone001, connection_ClusterGate418To401 (Family Zhin)
      B = Zone002, connection_ClusterGate418To404 (Zyarth's Dominion I)

    Zyarth's Dominion I:
      Nhuut gate = Zone005, connection_ClusterGate404To418

    Every gate/accelerator prop retains its vanilla position and rotation. Deliberately, the
    galaxy macro contains no destination connections at all. This removes every inherited
    sandbox route while preserving the gate landmarks used as the screenplay's reference frame.
